<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Deceuninck buys Alcoa extrusion unit.</title>
<headline>Belgian Deceuninck buys Alcoa extrusion unit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian PVC profiles producer Deceuninck NV said on Tuesday that it had reached agreement with U.S. aluminium producer Alcoa to buy Alcoa unit  Dayton Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>Dayton Technologies, based in Monroe, Ohio, is one of the largest U.S. companies active in the extrusion of plastic door- and window profiles.</p>
<p>No financial details were given.  </p>
<p>Dayton Technologies employs 300 people.</p>
<p>Deceuninck employs 892 and had 1996 turnover of 5.87 billion Belgian francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
